{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552074-w5-crinos-house-rules","id":1552074,"title":"W5 Crinos House Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-05T07:46:25-07:00","id":1552074,"title":"W5 Crinos House Rules","content":"Because I keep hearing people say the reason the crinos form is on a timer is due to how werewolf movies work, let's ACTUALLY base it on those.<br /> <br /> If you have seen any of the werewolf movie classics (The Howling, Dog Soldiers, American Werewolf in London, Company of the Wolves, etc.), you know that the werewolf transformation is not just a couple of minutes. It is the whole night.<br /> <br /> So let's use that.<br /> <br /> <b>Revised Crinos mechanics</b><ul><li>Stats stay the same.</li> <li>Crinos can only be used once the sun goes down.</li> <li>You are in full control; You can use gifts and weapons freely.</li> <li>Once you take Crinos, you cannot shift out of it until the sun has risen. Even if you get knocked out or killed, you will remain in crinos.</li> <li>Once the sun rises, you automatically shift out of Crinos. Even if you are knocked out or dead.</li> </ul><br /> This reflects the way werewolves work in movies, offering the players a risk vs reward scenario to deal with. As well as offering additional challenges/benefits based on location.<br /> <br /> For example, you cannot access Crinos during the summer in Scandinavia. The sun simply never goes down enough to allow it. But during the winter, you end up staying in Crinos until 9 am.<br /> <br /> The point is to offer the players control over their strategy, while staying true to the form of werewolf people have wanted in WoD for years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T09:38:27-07:00","id":1552076,"title":"","content":"I think another part of W5's restrictions on Crinos was that it also served as an excuse to not have Gifts that built on it, like Invocation of the Pharaohs, Gift of the Spriggan, or Warp Frenzy. Because if people lose their minds over Crinos not being restricted, it's also likely that they would crash out at the notion that Crinos is not the end point of Garou power and lethality, but rather than beginning of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T14:41:26-07:00","id":1552078,"title":"","content":"Im still unconvinced that crisis needs to be on a timer. Not in the least because hispo is an option.<br /> <br /> That said this does work better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T16:04:42-07:00","id":1552081,"title":"","content":"I have some thoughts about the initial premises... but I'll save those unless asked for them.<br /> <br /> As far as the rule? It's probably better than base W5 at a glance (the timer, like many things lifted from CofD games, doesn't seem to understand why those work in the CofD).<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure I'd really like it beyond that. The risk-reward is nearly impossible for the players or the player characters to reasonably judge. So much of the risk is ST fiat (aka how hard it will be on your character to make the rest of the night without being able to leave Crinos), it's the kind of mechanic that tends to make players far more uncertain and risk-averse than actually makes them feel rewarded for taking calculated risks. In the hands of a skilled ST that really knows what they're doing, it would be fun.. but that's because you have an ideal ST running it. For well meaning but new STs? This is the kind of mechanic that can send a game off the rails really quickly.<br /> <br /> I think it would be better if you added some sort of dial that helps the players (and ideally something that has some IC aspect so it doesn't feel like metagaming to make optimal choices) gauge the risk; which also helps STs ensure they're communicating the risks clearly and guide their own actions so that they keep to the risk level set. This is the kind of thing where H5's danger mechanic could actually be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T16:04:59-07:00","id":1552082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552074-w5-crinos-house-rules?p=1552078#post1552078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im still unconvinced that crisis needs to be on a timer. Not in the least because hispo is an option.<br /> <br /> That said this does work better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the same opinion, but I also understand that people want a more 'traditional' werewolf experience.<br /> <br /> However, the 'crinos should only be a few turns because that's more like werewolf movies' is not correct. The horror in the movies is that the rampage takes all night and only ends as the sun rises. So I wanted to depict the horror of being stuck as a monster all night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T16:12:49-07:00","id":1552084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552074-w5-crinos-house-rules?p=1552081#post1552081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be better if you added some sort of dial that helps the players (and ideally something that has some IC aspect so it doesn't feel like metagaming to make optimal choices) gauge the risk; which also helps STs ensure they're communicating the risks clearly and guide their own actions so that they keep to the risk level set. This is the kind of thing where H5's danger mechanic could actually be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example of what you mean by a dial? The general premise is to be 'true to classical werewolves' while still offering players a sense of control. I should note that every other form is free to access and shift out of.<br /> <br /> Within W5's Rage rules, there isn't really much room to play with the power vs loss of control in frenzy dynamic Legacy had for crinos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T16:34:26-07:00","id":1552088,"title":"","content":"I mentioned H5's danger tracker as an example... the ST sets a base &quot;risk&quot; rating, and it goes up or down based on PC actions. If the PCs are facing off against foes where popping Crinos isn't inherently a problem (like, say, other werewolves) in an isolated area near their main territory so there's basically no risk of being seen or harming innocents, you start at 0. Though the fight could always go in weird directions that draws attention. Getting into a fight with some government sponsored hunters in the middle of a city where there's lots of cameras and people between you and a safe spot to hide until sunrise could be a 5 (or whatever), and could go down if players take actions to help mitigate things. The number doesn't really matter (though you can make it matter if you want, it could be the difficulty of mitigating actions), the communication factor does. Setting the base level makes sure the ST is thinking about what the risks are going to be in the scene, and being able to toss down a number doesn't spoil any surprises while leaving the players feeling more empowered by knowing what kind of situation they're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T06:43:20-07:00","id":1552100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552074-w5-crinos-house-rules?p=1552088#post1552088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned H5's danger tracker as an example... the ST sets a base &quot;risk&quot; rating, and it goes up or down based on PC actions. If the PCs are facing off against foes where popping Crinos isn't inherently a problem (like, say, other werewolves) in an isolated area near their main territory so there's basically no risk of being seen or harming innocents, you start at 0. Though the fight could always go in weird directions that draws attention. Getting into a fight with some government sponsored hunters in the middle of a city where there's lots of cameras and people between you and a safe spot to hide until sunrise could be a 5 (or whatever), and could go down if players take actions to help mitigate things. The number doesn't really matter (though you can make it matter if you want, it could be the difficulty of mitigating actions), the communication factor does. Setting the base level makes sure the ST is thinking about what the risks are going to be in the scene, and being able to toss down a number doesn't spoil any surprises while leaving the players feeling more empowered by knowing what kind of situation they're in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yeah, that would be perfect for it.<br /> <br /> Shouldn't be hard to add, just add a gradient from 'safe' to 'veil breachy.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}